=encoding utf8

=head1 NAME

std/data/csv - CSV/TSV and delimited text data handling.

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  from std/data/csv import CSV;
  from std/io import Path;

  let csv := new CSV(
    headers: true,
    sep_char: ",",
  );

  let rows := csv.load( Path.tempfile() );

  let reader := csv.open( new Path("people.csv") );
  for ( let row in reader ) {
    say( row{name} );
  }

  let writer := csv.open_writer( new Path("people-out.csv") );
  writer.write_header( [ "name", "age" ] );
  writer.write_row( { name: "Ada", age: 32 } );
  writer.close();

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This module provides CSV-style parsing and writing backed by the runtime.
Its options are designed so the same API can also handle TSV and other
character-delimited formats.

=head2 Exports

=over

=item C<CSV>

Constructor options include:
C<sep_char>, C<quote_char>, C<escape_char>, C<eol>, C<binary>,
C<always_quote>, C<allow_whitespace>, C<blank_is_undef>,
C<empty_is_undef>, C<quote_empty>, C<quote_space>, C<quote_null>,
C<verbatim>, C<headers>, C<columns>, C<encoding>, C<append>,
C<skip_empty_rows>, C<comment_char>, C<skip_lines>, C<trim_headers>,
C<lowercase_headers>, C<rename_headers>, C<duplicate_headers>,
C<ragged>, C<fill_value>, C<types>, C<parsers>, C<formatters>,
C<defaults>, C<required_columns>, C<unknown_columns>, and C<on_error>.

Instance methods:

=over

=item * C<decode(text)>

Parse a whole string into an Array of rows. With C<headers: true>, rows
are returned as Dicts.

=item * C<decode_report(text)>

Decode while collecting parse errors instead of throwing immediately.
Returns a Dict with C<rows> and C<errors>.

=item * C<encode(rows)>

Encode rows into a delimited text string.

=item * C<encode_row(row)>

Encode a single row as delimited text.

=item * C<load(path)>

Read and parse a full file from a C<std/io> C<Path>.

=item * C<load_report(path)>

Load while collecting parse errors instead of throwing immediately.

=item * C<dump(path, rows)>

Write rows to a C<std/io> C<Path>.

=item * C<open(path)>

Open a streaming reader and return a C<CSVReader>.

=item * C<open_writer(path, options?)>

Open a streaming writer and return a C<CSVWriter>.

=item * C<sniff(text_or_path)>

Guess delimiter and likely header presence.

=item * C<transpose(rows)>

Transpose a table represented as nested Arrays.

=item * C<< dump_table(path, dbh, table, options?) >>

Export a database table through C<std/db> to a delimited file.

=item * C<< dump_query(path, dbh, sql, bind?, options?) >>

Export the results of an arbitrary SQL query through C<std/db>.

=item * C<< load_table(path, dbh, table, options?) >>

Import a delimited file into a database table. Supports creating the
table first when requested, plus batched transactional inserts and
column mapping.

=back

=item C<CSVReader>

Streaming reader returned by C<CSV.open>.

Methods:

=over

=item * C<next_array()>

=item * C<next_dict()>

=item * C<next()>

=item * C<all_array()>, C<all_dict()>

=item * C<headers()>

=item * C<columns()>, C<set_columns(columns)>

=item * C<row_number()>

=item * C<skip_lines(count)>

=item * C<errors()>

=item * C<close()>

=item * C<to_Iterator()>

Returns an iterator function suitable for C<for> loops. It yields Dict
rows when headers/columns are configured; otherwise it yields Array
rows.

=back

=item C<CSVWriter>

Streaming writer returned by C<CSV.open_writer>.

Methods:

=over

=item * C<write_header(columns?)>

=item * C<write_row(row)>

=item * C<print_row(row)>

=item * C<columns()>

=item * C<row_number()>

=item * C<close()>

=back

=back

